Skia: no pcs("aapcs-vfp") stage ABI for GCC on 32-bit ARM

The highp/lowp raster pipeline passes r,g,b,a between stages through a Stage
function-pointer type marked __attribute__((pcs("aapcs-vfp"))). With GCC and
-mfloat-abi=softfp the stage functions and the calls through that pointer type do
not agree on where the vectors go, so every 4-pixel group gets other lanes' and
channels' values: linear gradients, CSS masks and colour filters are drawn as
vertical stripes. Use the attribute only with clang; GCC keeps the NEON stages
with its default ABI (output identical to SKRP_CPU_SCALAR).

--- a/Source/ThirdParty/skia/src/opts/SkRasterPipeline_opts.h
+++ b/Source/ThirdParty/skia/src/opts/SkRasterPipeline_opts.h
@@ -1520,7 +1520,10 @@
 
 // Any custom ABI to use for all (non-externally-facing) stage functions?
 // Also decide here whether to use narrow (compromise) or wide (ideal) stages.
-#if defined(SK_CPU_ARM32) && defined(SKRP_CPU_NEON)
+// webOS browser: only with clang. GCC (softfp, -mfpu=neon) does not give the Stage function-pointer type the
+// same pcs("aapcs-vfp") convention as the stage functions, so r,g,b,a arrive in the wrong registers: gradients,
+// masks and colour filters come out as 4-pixel stripes. Without it GCC keeps the NEON code with its own ABI.
+#if defined(SK_CPU_ARM32) && defined(SKRP_CPU_NEON) && defined(__clang__)
     // This lets us pass vectors more efficiently on 32-bit ARM.
     // We can still only pass 16 floats, so best as 4x {r,g,b,a}.
     #define ABI __attribute__((pcs("aapcs-vfp")))
